    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0278" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.917/5694: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stewart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-14T10:30:00-06:00">December 14, 1943—10:30
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 17—3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–513. For the Foreign Economic Administration.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d258-f1"/>
                    Reference Department’s circular airgram of November 13, 1943, 12:10 p.m.<anchor
                        n="32" xml:id="d258-f2"/> and Department’s circular telegram of December 10,
                    10 a.m.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d258-f3"/> Also Department’s circular airgram of
                    November 13, 1943, 12:20 p.m.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d258-f4"/></p>
                <p>The Country Agency states that in view of certain discrepancies caused by local
                    banking regulations affecting commodities exportable from the United States
                    under general license, it will require import recommendations for all
                    commodities exported to this country. The <pb facs="0279" n="267" xml:id="pg267"
                    /> following is quoted from the Country Agency’s letter of December 10, 1943 to
                    the Embassy: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“…<anchor n="35" xml:id="d258-f5"/> please take notice that effective
                            immediately all commodities that have been withdrawn from the
                            Decentralization Plan including those commodities listed in Export
                            Bulletin No. 125,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d258-f6"/> will be subject to
                            Import Recommendations.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>A verbal exception to this requirement was received to wit newsprint and orders
                    for $25.00 or less.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d258-f1" n="31" xml:id="d258-f1-content">
                <p>The Office of Economic Warfare (formerly the Board of Economic Warfare) was
                    consolidated into the Foreign Economic Administration, September 25, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d258-f2" n="32" xml:id="d258-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg131">p. 131</ref>.</p>
            </note>
